EctoPad iOS audio follow-up, 2026-08-13

- activate an AVAudioSession in playback mode before opening SDL audio;
- request Prime's 32 kHz source rate and a 10 ms hardware I/O buffer while
  continuing to accept the actual device rate reported by iOS;
- initially restored the vendored SoXR variable-rate voice resampler, then
  removed it from the live pull path after physical logs proved it converted
  temporary Amuse starvation into permanent end-of-input;
- clamp the final float stream at [-1, 1];
- persist bounded audio diagnostics: actual route/rate/buffer/channels,
  output-ready queue depth, underruns, peak, and clipped-sample count;
- log frontend, Amuse, and streamed-DSP sources independently, comparing
  discontinuities within each stereo channel instead of across L/R samples;
- restore the previously audible direct Amuse pull path. The rejected SoXR
  build had 193 voices marked running while `amuse=0.000`; streamed DSP was
  nonzero until it ended, after which total output became zero;
- decode frontend RSF one nibble/sample at a time. The iPad conversion asks
  for alternating 682/683-frame chunks; the former pair-only loop dropped
  every odd tail while advancing the cursor, causing gaps and state drift.

This complements the restored DSP stream mixer. It deliberately does not copy
SunPad's Dolphin/recompiler-specific 12x guest-timebase workaround.

An early diagnostic compared interleaved L/R neighbors and therefore
overstated its discontinuity counts; it was corrected before the final deploy.
The odd-frame decoder defect is established directly by the pair-only source
loop and the observed alternating 682/683-frame requests. Accurate voice
pitch/rate conversion is now explicit debt until starvation and EOF can be
signaled separately. Audible acceptance remains required.

The final listening pass still found a brief aberration at the frontend-to-
asteroid/planet transition. A bounded 320-frame transition ramp was tested and
physically rejected because it did not remove the aberration; it was removed
before the final build. The smooth limiter remains after the complete frontend
+ Amuse + DSP-stream sum. Source/mixer behavior at the transition remains open.
